# Ubuntu packages and sudo

This workspace runs on **Ubuntu**. Prefer real open-source tools when they clearly help (OCR, image conversion, codecs, system services, apt packages, and similar).

## Do not run sudo yourself

- The agent cannot reliably use `sudo` (password required).
- Do **not** invent workarounds that skip a standard package when the package is the right tool.
- Do **not** silently fall back to brittle alternatives without asking first.

## Ask clearly

When a package or system install would help, **stop and ask** the user to run the command. Be direct. Paste a copy-pasteable command, for example:

```bash
sudo apt-get install -y tesseract-ocr tesseract-ocr-eng
```

Keep the ask short: what you need, why (one line), and the exact command. After they confirm it is installed, continue.

## Prefer asking over improvising

If apt / a system binary is the clean path, ask. User-level installs without sudo are fine when they already work and fit the project.
